  "articleBody": "Not every wall ding needs a contractor, but certain drywall issues point to deeper problems or demand specialized finish tools to make your rooms look clean again.\n\nSigns It Is Time to Call a Professional:\n- Moisture damage or recurring soft spots: Stained or crumbly drywall must not just be patched; the underlying leak must be addressed first.\n- Large openings across stud bays: Gaps wider than a few inches require solid wood backing and structural support rather than mesh screens.\n- Openings near wiring or pipes: Cutting into walls with hidden mechanical lines risks safety and requires careful inspection.\n- Ceiling damage and sagging sheets: Overhead repairs fight gravity and require secure mechanical fastening to joists.\n- Matching existing wall texture: Blending a flat patch into knockdown or orange peel textures takes seasoned hand-tool technique.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start\nTake clear photos of the damaged area, note whether any plumbing or electrical work recently took place, and confirm if you have matching leftover paint. If your home has wall damage that needs solid backing and clean finishing, reach out to HH Remodeling LLC. Abraham Becerra and his crew handle drywall, framing, and interior painting throughout the greater Denver area. Call 303-505-0866 to schedule an on-site visit.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
